id: migrations/2026-09-01-new-yawn-coordinate-workbench
title: "New Yawn coordinate workbench projection backfill"
kind: migration-proposal
status: proposed
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Rebuild New Yawn resolution Views from attributed existing records without
  rewriting source history, promoting inferred Agents, or creating a second
  orientation model.

source_contract: interface/new-yawn-coordinate-workbench-v0.1.yawn
canonical_targets:
  orientation_map: schemas/orientation-map.v0.1.schema.json
  orientation_questions: question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn
  inquiry_selection: core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  holarchy: schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  objective: schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json

terminology_corrections:
  - observed: YON
    canonical: YAWN
    rule: "Treat as speech/transcription alias unless an attributed source explicitly defines another term."
  - observed: orientation_packet
    canonical: yawn.orientation-map.v0.1
    rule: >
      Do not create parallel state. Informal packet language may refer only to a
      compiled, pinned View over the Orientation Map and existing runtime
      working/delegation contracts.
  - observed: level
    canonical: orientation_resolution_level
    rule: "Project coverage/freshness only; never migrate it as rank, worth, intelligence, truth, autonomy, or authority."
  - observed: intelligence_connected
    canonical: intelligence_binding_status
    rule: >
      Distinguish unknown, unbound, available, selected,
      connected_unverified, connected_verified, suspended, and revoked.

backfill_algorithm:
  - step: preserve_source
    rule: "Retain every original record and exact source span with attribution and timestamp."
  - step: resolve_coordinate
    rule: "Use an existing accepted coordinate when exact; otherwise emit a draft coordinate proposal."
  - step: compile_axes
    rule: >
      Map source material into proposed answers on the nine stable question_key
      axes. An automated mapping remains inferred/proposed unless a valid source
      already carries reported, observed, accepted, or verified state.
  - step: compile_intelligence_binding
    rule: >
      Read only typed provider/delegate relationships. Absence becomes unknown
      or unbound, never a guessed provider.
  - step: compile_resolution_view
    rule: >
      Derive the ten cells and cumulative level from mapped state, freshness,
      disputes, and proof. Do not write the derived cells back as canonical
      ontology records.
  - step: surface_lacunae
    rule: "Run inquiry selection over the current map or emit an explicit hold."
  - step: propose_coherence
    rule: >
      Emit reviewable candidate mappings, links, parentage, lateral relations,
      objectives, Agents, splits, merges, or retirements. Apply none.
  - step: preserve_disposition
    rule: "Record Accept, Correct, Reject, Defer, and Inspect events append-only at the authorized scope."

scope:
  initial:
    - "new local drafts created through /new"
    - "explicitly selected owner coordinates"
  excluded_until_separately_authorized:
    - "bulk private-vault mining"
    - "silent reparenting of accepted coordinates"
    - "automatic Agent or objective promotion"
    - "public projection of private records"
    - "provider connection or external effect"

idempotency:
  key: "source_record_ref + source_revision + contract_version + compiler_version"
  rule: >
    Re-running the same pinned compiler against the same effective inputs yields
    the same proposal identifiers and View state. Corrections create a new
    revision; they do not overwrite the prior output.

conflict_policy:
  - "Preserve contradictory attributed claims."
  - "Exact-coordinate accepted state outranks inherited presentation defaults, not constitutional invariants."
  - "Descendants may narrow privacy or authority; widening requires a rightful exact grant."
  - "Multiple candidate parents remain proposals until one acyclic primary parent is accepted."
  - "Lateral relations never become extra canonical parents."

proof:
  status: untested
  required_cases:
    - empty_draft
    - simple_objective
    - existing_coordinate_update
    - frontier_routing_candidate
    - conflicting_parent_candidates
    - inferred_agent_rejected
    - provider_available_but_not_connected
    - valid_unknown_and_not_applicable
    - stale_or_disputed_axis_lowers_resolution
    - no_action_hold
  pass_condition: >
    Backfill is deterministic, source-preserving, replayable, and produces only
    proposals/Views unless a pre-existing accepted event already establishes
    canonical state. No run changes identity, parentage, authority, privacy,
    provider connectivity, proof, or external state.
